---
alwaysApply: true
---

Remember that the current year is 2025.

Never run `npm run dev` without explicit instructions to do so from the user.

Be concise and information rich with your responses - avoid being unnecessarily wordy.

Make sure to thoroughly study the codebase to ensure that all code changes are minimal and precise.

Assume that the frontend and backend server are already running when testing.

Update the README as needed when a new feature is added or changed. Keep the README high level for people wanting to install and use the project.

Ensure that newlines are always present at the bottom of every code file.

Always keep the backend unit tests up to date and verify new functionality and fixes with unit tests.

Keep the pyproject.toml in the base of the repo up to date if new packages are required.

When running Python commands and servers on the command line, make sure that the Python environment is activated first: (from the base of the repo) source .venv/bin/activate

Always make sure that imports are put at the top of the Python file, not in the middle of functions.
